HTML Practice Examples

Here is a simple practice guide covering HTML Elements, Attributes, Images, Quotations, Hyperlinks, Lines, and Lists.

1. HTML Elements

An HTML element usually has an opening tag, content, and a closing tag.

<h1>Welcome to HTML</h1>
<p>This is my first HTML paragraph.</p>

Examples:

<h1>Heading</h1>
<h2>Sub Heading</h2>
<p>Paragraph</p>
<b>Bold Text</b>
<i>Italic Text</i>
2. HTML Attributes

Attributes provide extra information about an HTML element.

<p title="This is a paragraph">Hello HTML</p>

Common attributes:

id
class
style
title
href
src
alt
width
height

Example:

<p id="para1" class="text">Hello World</p>
3. HTML Images

The <img> tag is used to display an image.

<img src="image.jpg" alt="My Image">

With width and height:

<img src="image.jpg" alt="Nature Image" width="300" height="200">

Practice:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Images</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>My Image</h1>

    <img src="flower.jpg" alt="Flower Image" width="300">

</body>
</html>
4. HTML Quotations
<blockquote>

Used for a longer quotation.

<blockquote>
    Learning HTML is the first step toward web development.
</blockquote>
<q>

Used for a short quotation.

<p>My teacher says, <q>Practice makes perfect.</q></p>
<abbr>

Used for abbreviations.

<p><abbr title="HyperText Markup Language">HTML</abbr> is used to create web pages.</p>
5. HTML Hyperlinks

The <a> tag creates a hyperlink.

<a href="https://www.google.com">Google</a>

Open the link in a new tab:

<a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">
    Open Google
</a>

Email link:

<a href="mailto:example@gmail.com">Send Email</a>

Phone link:

<a href="tel:+919876543210">Call Me</a>
6. HTML Horizontal Line

The <hr> tag creates a horizontal line.

<h1>My Website</h1>

<hr>

<p>Welcome to my website.</p>

Example:

<h2>About Me</h2>
<p>I am a web developer.</p>

<hr>

<h2>My Skills</h2>
<p>HTML, CSS, JavaScript</p>
7. HTML Lists
Unordered List

Uses bullet points.

<ul>
    <li>HTML</li>
    <li>CSS</li>
    <li>JavaScript</li>
</ul>

Output:

HTML
CSS
JavaScript
Ordered List

Uses numbers.

<ol>
    <li>HTML</li>
    <li>CSS</li>
    <li>JavaScript</li>
</ol>

Output:

HTML
CSS
JavaScript
Ordered List with Different Type
<ol type="A">
    <li>HTML</li>
    <li>CSS</li>
    <li>JavaScript</li>
</ol>
Description List
<dl>
    <dt>HTML</dt>
    <dd>HyperText Markup Language</dd>

    <dt>CSS</dt>
    <dd>Cascading Style Sheets</dd>
</dl>
